  "title": "Week 3: San Sebastián 🌊",
  "date": "2026-01-22T22:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Week 3: San Sebastián 🌊\n\nAfter a 5-hour train ride, I finally arrived in Hendaye. Fun fact: the name sounds a lot like \"Hentai,\" but luckily the \"H\" is silent! 🙊 This is the gateway to Spain, where I hopped on the Euskotren—a charming narrow-gauge railway—to reach San Sebastián. 🚉\n\nWindow view\n\nBy the time I pulled into San Sebastián, it was late and raining. 🌧️ The humid air and the city's initial vibe actually reminded me a lot of Thailand! 🇹🇭\n\nBridge\n\nMy first meal? A simple salad paired with my first-ever Dr. Pepper. Honestly? Not a fan. 🥤🚫\n\nDr. Pepper\n\nCity Vibes & AI Guides 🤖\n\nThe next morning, the weather cleared up beautifully. This is exactly the European city aesthetic I was hoping for! ✨\n\nRainbow\n\nThe local beaches are a canvas; you can find artists creating intricate sand drawings that change day by day. 🏖️🎨\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| First day | Second day |\n\nI used Doubao (豆包) and Gemini as my personal tour guides while wandering the streets. 📱\n\n| Day 1 | Day 2 |\n|-|-|\n| Doubao | Gemini |\n\nThe verdict? Doubao is more chatty with information, while Gemini feels more intuitive to interact with. However, you always have to fact-check! Doubao tried to convince me a regular tree was a sculpture. I’m pretty sure it was just... a tree. 🌳😂\n\nAnd the network signal was not very stable. Sometime you lost connection while shopping. 🛍️\n\nSurfing & Game of Thrones ⚔️🏄‍♂️\n\nSan Sebastián also served as a filming location for HBO's Game of Thrones. Walking along the coast, the rugged landscape feels instantly familiar. 🐉\n\nland\n\nAs a huge surfing fan, I was in heaven. Even at 15°C, the water was filled with surfers catching waves. 🏄‍♂️❄️ The Old Town is packed with cool surf shops and local character.\n\n| Surfers in the mist | Surf Shop Vibes |\n|-|-|\n| Surfers | surf board store|\n\nLocal Flavors & Fond Farewells 🍤\n\nForget giant malls—this city is all about small kiosks, cozy sandwich spots, and bars serving incredible Pintxos. Finally, some fresh seafood! 😋\n\n| Fresh Bites | Pintxos Paradise |\n|-|-|\n| Fresh Bites | Pintxos Paradise |\n\nMy stay at the hostel was amazing. Before checking out, I left a little note featuring the game I’m developing: Grandpa's Bee Haven. 🐝🎮\n\nnote\n\nI hope a fellow traveler finds it and gives it a play!",
